{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1487400-share-your-homebrewed-places-that-aren\u2019t","id":1487400,"title":"Share your homebrewed Places-That-Aren\u2019t!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-21T10:17:59-07:00","id":1487400,"title":"Share your homebrewed Places-That-Aren\u2019t!","content":"Here, we can share our homebrewed Places-That-Aren\u2019t, the area\u2019s of the Shadow that correspond to no geographical locale!<br /> <br /> Mine:<br /> <br /> 1)Granted, the game only lasted three sessions before dying, and the PCs never managed to get there, but I had the pack investigating a series of ritualistic murders in various old, rundown and abandoned churches by a cult loyal to a covey of murder-spirits. The spirits were using the same churches again and again and again, and, in the Shadow, these churches became one place, an upside down cathedral where spirits walk on the floors high above and hunt lesser spirits by using extremely alien equivalents of fishing poles. Where the altar would be was the man this covey was trying to Hive-Claim: the \u2018god\u2019 the cult believed would soon arise.<br /> <br /> What about you guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-22-2022, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T10:01:12-07:00","id":1487488,"title":"","content":"2)The hospital\u2019s cancer ward had a history of patients dying. It soon became a thing of urban legend, and eventually the ward caught fire. The hospital soon shut down...but the cancer ward <i>kept going</i>, on into infinity.<br /> <br /> If one enters the <i>Hisil</i> and goes in said hospital, they find it full of forlorn, bitter, angry spirits bewildered by their food-source going away. But if one enters the cancer ward from within the Shadow, one enters another place altogether.<br /> <br /> The cancer ward is a Place-That-Isn\u2019t, an endless series of hallways with flickering fluorescent lights, low levels of baking radiation, and screams coming at the most inopportune moments from behind doors that can\u2019t be opened by mundane strength, alone. Walking lumps of tumor, pus and human hair can be found nesting in hallways, and insects swarm in ventilation-ducts.<br /> <br /> If one could find the cancer ward\u2019s center (which would require supernatural methods) one would find oneself in the ward\u2019s head doctor\u2019s office. Here squats a rail-thin spirit, flesh melted off by radioactivity, fingers lost yet still trying to write reports. It\u2019s glad you\u2019re here. Just in time for treatment...<br /> <br /> 3)Gobekli Tepe (a very real place, by the way) hosts a Place-That-Isn\u2019t of mammoth proportions. It is also a wildly powerful locus, with Uratha words of binding everywhere, albeit supernaturally hidden from human eyesight.<br /> <br /> The oldest known temple in the world, since its rediscovery Gobekli Tepe has become of deep interest to virtually every splat, as the site holds Mysteries to almost all of them. It is the Uratha-specific mysteries we explore here, today.<br /> <br /> Sidestepping in Gobekli Tepe <i>immediately</i> shunts a werewolf into the Place-That-Isn\u2019t a primeval forest with trees so tall no matter how hard one tries one can never breach the canopy. Ancient spirits of extinct megafauna roam here, their hides cracked and sickly green light shining out from within. Their eyes are milky cataracts and they do not speak, even in the First Tongue.<br /> <br /> The forest is of immense size, though only the outermost edges are accessible to any but the mightiest Or cleverest of packs. Guarding the forest\u2019s primordial interior are giant stone sentinels, spirits bound by strictures both Infernal and divine to prevent any from going further in.<br /> <br /> What lies within? No one knows for sure, but, under the light of the full moon, strange, hulking shapes can be barely discerned in the distance, performing what appears to be a strange dance, with piping flutes and beating drums breaking the forest\u2019s normal aura of silence.<br /> <br /> 4)Even Wounds can have Places-That-Aren\u2019t, terrifying holes in reality where the very worst aspects of reality fester and boil. The Deeremonte Estate is just such a place.<br /> <br /> Home to the Deeremonte family, known for generations as inbred cannibals, this house has been abandoned since WWI. Horrible things happened to travels in there, atrocities of staggering inhumanity. And these horrifying things kept happening for generations, til, at WWI, the local police got up the gumption to get rid of the family.<br /> <br /> The Deeremonte Estate is a creepy place, to be sure, an abandoned, crumbling edifice. But, if someone enters it from the Shadow Realm, they might never leave.<br /> <br /> The Place-That-Isn\u2019t inside the Estate is the house at its gory height, with a never-ending psychodrama of the site\u2019s most awful events on perpetual replay. Wounded spirits enact the roles of the Deeremonte family, while a Maeltinet takes on the role as \u201cPapa\u201d.<br /> <br /> At the very bottommost part of the Place-That-Isn\u2019t, corresponding roughly with the Estate\u2019s basement, is a crack in the Earth, going...somewhere. The Maeltinet comes here, sometimes, to listen alien whispers on it can hear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-22-2022, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T20:31:13-07:00","id":1487537,"title":"","content":"This is a very old piece, but here ya go<br /> <br /> Number 5 I suppose!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city\"> Places-That-Aren't: The Forge-City - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Another jewel of mine that I recently rediscovered, I hope you like it! ________________________ The Forge-City There are many Places-That-Aren't, some little </div> </div> </div>","signature":"Another jewel of mine that I recently rediscovered, I hope you like it! ________________________ The Forge-City There are many Places-That-Aren't, some little","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:22:12-07:00","id":1487603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1487400-share-your-homebrewed-places-that-aren\u2019t?p=1487537#post1487537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very old piece, but here ya go<br /> <br /> Number 5 I suppose!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/475321-places-that-aren-t-the-forge-city\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...the-forge-city</a></div> </div> </div> </div>For the curious, the above-mentioned Place-That-Isn\u2019t is:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Forge-City <br /> <br /> There are many Places-That-Aren't, some little more than closets that don't exist in the real world, or are small spaces that are a bit larger on the inside than out. Others are quite large, one being an entire floor that's not there, or even entire realms of their own within the Shadow itself. The Forge City is one such realm, one of fire and smoke and steel. Connected to the administrative office of an abandoned automotive factory in the Shadow, opening the door to the office leads to a vast and incredible realm that defies mortal logic. The Forge City is a massive collection of foundries filled with white hot materials processing tirelessly, smokestacks billowing black smoke into the midnight black sky, pits of molten Essence dotting the landscape, factories filled with machinery endlessly operating nonstop, labyrinthine streets of basalt snake in between buildings, broken only by Essence Pits or vents that which erupt into pillars of burning energy. As stated before, this realm is vast, extending for miles around in all directions, though the very city limits seem to be a circular rock wall that extends vertically in the air eternally. Another feature of this realm is that the only light to be seen comes from the city itself and it's assorted structures, as the there is no day/night cycle in this realm, only the smoke filled obsidian sky.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, this Place-That-Isn't is quite antagonistic to newcomers that haven't quite adjusted to such a harsh environment. For Uratha it quickly comes apparent just how inhospitable this place is, the air is burning hot and choked with smoke, making breathing a challenge at best and seems to burn the very essence in their bodies, inflicting a point of lethal damage every hour as well as the loss of a point of Essence. Fortunately Essence is immensely plentiful in the Forge City, the trick is to be willing to endure high levels of pain in order to harvest it. Essentially the entire realm is one giant locus, it's bounty in the form of it's rivers of molten slag and geysers of intense energy, one merely needs to reach out and reap the rewards... at the cost of their flesh that is. for every lethal damage sustained from these sources the werewolf ( or non native spirit) gains one essence. Once the werewolf has remained in the City for 24 hours they will have adapted to the realm and find that the air becomes much more breathable and the temperature, while uncomfortable, is more bearable and no longer scorches the werewolf. They still take damage from harvesting Essence from the vents and pools, but they gain 2 Essence per point of lethal, same with non native spirits who have adapted.<br /> <br /> While the Forge City itself is ripe with an abundance of Essence, the Shadow locale it is connected to is not. the Abandoned factory is essentially a Barrens from so many years of inactivity, the flow of Essence long having dried up and dissipated. How the Forge City has managed to thrive is both as interesting as it is simple. during the late 20's all the way through the 60's that particular factory had gained quite a bit of fame as it manufactured everything from automobile parts to weapons and ammunition to fighter jet components to even lesser items such as baby bottles and children toys. For so many decades the factory had become one of the symbols of what the American people could engineer, and the emotional and conceptual energies tied to the factory bloomed, forming a locus tied to the resonance of industry and production inside the head executive's office within the administrative wing of the building, a locus that rapidly gained strength and grew to a font of Essence of legendary proportions.<br /> <br /> During the early days life was good for the spirits of the factory, and Essence was immensely plentiful, with more than enough to go around. Even without the pesky Uratha to police it, the factory was quite harmonious and there were few disruptions, the spirit of the factory itself made sure of that. Christening itself the Foreman the Factory-spirit, now a powerful Incarnae of Industry, oversaw that it's fellow spirits performed their natural tasks quickly and efficiently, for doing well within the Shadow ensured rich new Essence to flow from the world of Light to feed them all even more. During this time the Foreman also worked to create a place ideal for spirits such as itself and it's brood, a space where they could dwell and never worry about the meddlesome Uratha who would surely one day come calling, or the avarious spirits of greed and exploitation that began worming their way into it's Court. By the mid 60's it finally finished it's grand task of creating it's own realm within the Shadow, transforming the office containing the locus into it's own self sustained, self sufficient space, a realm of metal and fire and industrial fantasy.<br /> <br /> This event couldn't of happened a moment too soon as not long after the factory's shadow began to weaken. What had happened as that over the years the factory's importance began to lessen and the demand for it's products became less and less as other, more attractive forms of business began appearing. The Foreman saw this and desperately tried to aid the factory by creating more products with it's Influence, and for a time this did indeed help give the factory a great edge over it's competition, but in doing so it caught the attentions of a local pack of Iron Masters and for the first time in over four decades the denizens of the factory had to defend themselves against the accursed children of Father Wolf. While the spirits and the Foreman fought fiercely, the Uratha were no careless spirits starving for Essence, and they were able to push the spirits to the brink of eradication within a few short days. Terrified of what was happening and enraged at the Uratha who dared to interfere with it's agenda, the Foreman quickly saw no other choice for survival and ushered the surviving members of it's Court into the infant Place-That-Wasn't. After the last spirit fled inside, the Incarnae too retreated within and sealed the entrance behind it, placing itself and it's court out of the werewolve's reach.<br /> <br /> Since then the factory has long fallen into disrepair. As the Foreman couldn't aid it's dying factory with it's Influence it quickly went bankrupt and was then shut down. Soon after the Shadow of and around the factory whither and slowly began to die, becoming a moderately large Barren. As for the Forge City itself it has been thriving vastly since it's isolation, becoming a sort of spiritual Galapagos as it's spirits have evolved largely without human influence (save for a few rare occasions) , and in fact actually has been growing as it's pocket space seems to be expanding. the reason for this continued prosperity is due to the City partially being kept alive due to the occasional influx of new spirits that are drawn to the factory when the door to the Forge City is opened, acting as a Siren's call. These new spirits help refresh the pools of Essence within the the City and helps inform it's &quot;citizens&quot; of the changes that have happened in the outside world, and eventually these newcomers are added to the fold and gamut of the Forge City's population, furthering the growth of this strange &quot;paradise&quot;. </div> </div> </div>The above is not my work, instead being entirely designed by Korogra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T10:16:56-07:00","id":1487614,"title":"","content":"6)Not every Place-That-Isn\u2019t has meaning. Some were abandoned, while others formed for seemingly no reason at all. The Detroit Temple is one such Place-That-Isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Perpetually on the northern outskirts of Detroit\u2019s <i>Hisil</i>, reaching the Detroit Temple is a somewhat difficult matter, as one must be in exactly the right frame of mind and be pondering automobiles and the automotive industry while <i>in</i> that frame of mind. And that frame of mind is Apathy. To reach the Detroit Temple, one must not care if one reaches it. Otherwise, it\u2019s forever out of reach.<br /> <br /> The Detroit Temple looks like a cross between a car museum and a Catholic cathedral, adorned on the outside with automotive symbolism, of all kinds. The cathedral\u2019s doors stand wide open, and inside is....nothing. Just an empty space. Spirits refuse to go in willingly, but can\u2019t explain why. Uratha have explored the Detroit Temple a great many times, and find no use for it.<br /> <br /> However, if a mage used Mage Sight within the Detroit Temple such a mage would swiftly develop a very different opinion.<br /> <br /> 7)Mars. The red planet. If it has a Shadow of it\u2019s own, no one knows. But there <i>is</i> a Place-That-Isn\u2019t reflective of Mars, and it can only be found by aimlessly wandering NASA HQ after sundown.<br /> <br /> This Place-That-Isn\u2019t is a strange, dead landscape, embodying scientific fact, rather than pulp or science fiction. No John Carter, here. Furthermore, it\u2019s not even on Mars, being within Earth\u2019s Shadow.<br /> <br /> Dust elemental spirits rule the skies, and the two moons glare down like dead, unseeing eyes. Great earth elementals slowly creep across the land. And, every so often, an undead being glowing with power appears but briefly, and Uratha unlucky enough to witness these beings often go mad with induced visions, especially visions of Martian planetary angels.<br /> <br /> 8)The tribal totems inhabit hidden realms in the Shadow Realm, and Rabid Wolf is no exception.<br /> <br /> A terrifying eternal forest fire sends up vast clouds of soot that shut out the sky, leaving only fire and the light of painful doom to guide your way. Almost like a labyrinth, the fires seem to corral you ever deeper, drawing one to the apocalyptic center of this incendiary madness.<br /> <br /> Looming shapes, so burnt they can no longer be recognized, stumble through the cacophony, while stags coated in lesions urge interlopers ever forward in mangled human voices.<br /> <br /> At the very center squats a mound of bodies piled high, the bodies both gangrenous and aflame, the stench enough to floor even the hardiest werewolf. Atop this burning pile is the sizzling meat-puppet, a parody of a wolf carcass, animated by Rabid Wolf\u2019s indomitable will. It leers blindly at you, this perpetually dying <i>thing</i> and it shrieks your sins with demented glee.<br /> <br /> Chained all around it are werewolves who thought to spurn Rabid Wolf\u2019s truth, forever burning. They scream litanies of belief, their wills long ago broken.<br /> <br /> 9)The Cave is THE cave, a Shadow representation of caves everywhere, and the notions that monsters lurk below, scared away by the sun\u2019s harsh rays and the cleansing kiss of moonlit nights.<br /> <br /> One must be in a cavern system of considerable size, though one system is more desirable than another. One will eventually find a crack in the cavern walls, <i>just</i> big enough to allow a single person through. One crawls into the fissure and spends a cramped half hour of minimal movement, before popping through into <i>the</i> Cave.<br /> <br /> The Cave is a vast maze of tubes, chambers and waterways, that twists in on itself into a physically impossible manner.<br /> <br /> Here, in the dark, lurk fossil spirits of things dead for millions of years, a whole society of mute, forgotten, frozen spirits. And ruling above them all is a fragment of Bear, <i>the</i> bear-spirit, torn away in a fight with Father Wolf and crawling into this Cave to heal. It is angry and hungry and eager to escape, but it cannot. Bear herself would simply eat it or kill it: no returned apotheosis awaits this vengeful, bitter godling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-23-2022, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T19:23:14-07:00","id":1487828,"title":"","content":"10)A cult that worshipped an Eldritch thing trapped in the earth and stone practiced grisly rites for generations, slowly working to free the entity they called a deity.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, some Forsaken took care of the cult, but did not realize the entity\u2019s nearness to the surface after a hundred years or more of rituals has carved out a Place-That-Isn\u2019t, a \u201cwomb\u201d that will spawn it out from its prison.<br /> <br /> Resembling a biomechanical hellhole, forever an ever-diminishing spiral leading down, down, down to the creature itself...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T14:11:18-07:00","id":1487937,"title":"","content":"11)The House of Fear is located...<i>nowhere</i>. At least, nowhere in cosmology as werewolves understand it. It exists outside of the mortal world <i>and</i> the Shadow Realm, in a nebulous place Uratha can\u2019t easily quantify. Spirits cannot enter it, and know nothing of it. Physically finding it is impossible, as no amount of searching will uncover it.<br /> <br /> But it <i>can</i> be reached through a unique rite known only to very few packs. It shifts into what is somehow a \u2018different\u2019 Twilight, and following the wooded trail beyond to a gigantic, festering human corpse with an oak door carved into its stomach. Enter that door, and you enter the House of Fear.<br /> <br /> It a labyrinth, not a house, but the name persists. Spirits unlike anything werewolves are familiar with lurk here: minotaurs with cleaving axes, echoes of the future of the very packmates themselves, only antagonistic, even men made of curiously dull stone claiming to be of the fabled City of Atlantis that try to bar your progress.<br /> <br /> Solving the maze is hellishly difficult, but possible. At the far end is an archway, beyond that archway light so blinding and so alien to the Uratha they must either avert their gazes or go blind. Winged angels with bows of fire and swords of ice prevent further passage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T01:31:11-07:00","id":1488143,"title":"","content":"Have you ever heard of Null island? Funny real life story: the word 'null' is sometimes used to mean 'no information' rather than 'zero'. Sometimes machines don't understand that or how to accept that information is missing. This means that something located at 'null' is taken to mean the coordinates (0,0). This creates the illusion that things people, places, and things of all variety can be found in some obscure spot in the ocean.<br /> <br /> When I learned of that I thought back to werewolf: the forsaken. These are pictures of places that exist, just made to seem localized due to machine error. If perception can twist the Hisil out of proportion with the world, then what we have is a nexus of extradimensional pathways all across the world. If a Wound were to open there or a spirit noble open a travel business there, the story implications would be terrible. A spot of such opportunity and vulnerability. <br /> <br /> Of course, should a pack take that place then territory disputes are going to be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T09:43:30-07:00","id":1488180,"title":"","content":"Interesting!<br /> <br /> Anyhow, onwards and upwards.<br /> <br /> 12)The Place-That-Isn\u2019t for Death Wolf can only be reached through the largest of human graveyards, where the Resonance of death is at its strongest, yet the way cannot open if an Avernian Gate is open, strangely enough.<br /> <br /> Her realm is a somber forest in winter. Not the apocalyptic snow of some other Firstborn, but a gentle, pervading silence. Owl-spirits Nest here in huge numbers, and will occasionally allow strange \u201ccousins from Dis\u201d to nest with them.<br /> <br /> Stone resembling ancient shamans are really immobile spirits working dark rites to keep all ghosts from entering. It is as if Death Wolf is <i>very</i> concerned something from the Underworld might invade.<br /> <br /> Caves here are places to meditate and pray, though the religion in question can be whatever it happens to be. (One cave, in particular, is strewn with icons of Eastern Orthodox saints.)<br /> <br /> In the center of the Place-That-Isn\u2019t is a vast stone pillar hundreds of meters tall, upon the top of which rests a wolf of enormous proportions that, despite being alive, looks freshly dead. Death-spirits attend her, and murder-spirits protect her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 07-27-2022, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-28T21:12:07-07:00","id":1488316,"title":"","content":"13) red wolf\u2019s hidden palace in the shadow is urban in nature as to be expected, though the exact nature of the city is constantly shifting along a time line or perhaps several timelines that always start around the taming of electricity and wind up in one of the many futures that never were and yet could have been. The feel is something like a combination of Tomorrowland and San Andreas as the trapped souls of humans slain as prey in an Iron Master\u2019s sacred hunt go about false lives under the direction of spiritual tycoons and police, laboring in factories producing not products but ideas that might become seeds of change in.the flesh if planted in the right mind and businesses that seem to only exist for the sake of an eternal hunt. In the very center of this bizarre metropolis lies a massive wolf who always looks a little different every time you look at it, a patch of fur changes color or a scar appears that you swear wasn\u2019t there before. Red wolf watches her city change and so she understands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-08T18:52:14-07:00","id":1489521,"title":"","content":"14)Not all death-entities dwell in the Underworld or Duat. Death-spirits inhabit the Shadow Realm, not the lands of the dead and, in a place between places, have created a chapel to Death Wolf.<br /> <br /> Only reachable by traveling to the Shadow of highly specific graveyards in a highly specific order, the Chapel of Whispers is a cathedral made of bones and skulls. Murder-spirits serve as priests, and wear black robes stained with blood, while taxidermy-spirits keep warm near the barrow-fire crematoria on-site. The priests chant non-stop, swinging censers filled with burning straw, and perambulate the cathedral in a complete, highly circuitous route.<br /> <br /> The Shade Bishop is the lord of the Cathedral of Whispers, and is a horror that has never seen the sun. Pale as milk, with a grinning skull for a face, he trails behind himself with chains the few unlucky ghosts His Eminance has been able to capture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T09:33:26-07:00","id":1489645,"title":"","content":"15)In an industrial park in Russia there stands a great corroded stone doorframe, utterly unlike anything the Uratha have seen before. Here, it seems, despite not being a locus, one can walk through this doorway and enter a Place-That-Isn\u2019t out some nightmare.<br /> <br /> It is a maze of building, factories, water purification systems, dim alleys and winding streets, as if designed to get you lost. Eventually, you reach a choice: leave the city for the heavily forested wilderness beyond, or go deeper into the city.<br /> <br /> Going out of the city leads to a maze of thickly forested trees, tangled undergrowth and rivers suffering from industrial pollution. One\u2019s inner fury begins to build, and the pack may tear itself apart at any moment. They can keep going, after a time they enter a clearing with a vast stone wall separating the pack from whatever lay beyond. Climbing the wall is certainly possible, but...reaching the top might not be such a good idea. The landscape you see on the other side of the wall <i>makes no sense</i>, all wrong angles, shadows pointing the wrong way and more. Every Uratha who sees this place goes insane. Those who cross over are never seen again.<br /> <br /> Going deeper into the city is another matter altogether, as you eventually reach a bizarre commercial center, filled with dwarves from folklore selling things that can\u2019t be sold in the material realm. The prices? Memories. A droplet of one\u2019s blood, a rhyme. Russian Uratha have purchased <i>very</i> strange fetishes here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T09:50:04-07:00","id":1490036,"title":"","content":"16)Deep below Manhattan lie tunnels, only parts of which are in the material Realm. These tunnels snake about, parts of them in the Flesh, other parts in the Shadow. No loci exist at any point on this system, so only the most powerful werewolves have any hope to complete the circuit from start to finish.<br /> <br /> Such a werewolf, upon finishing the tunnels, would find himself in a Place-That-Isn\u2019t a perfect replica of the height of the Tammany Hall era of NYC. Bizarre <i>magath</i> endlessly reenact the events of the era, and seem to know nothing else.<br /> <br /> At the center of this madness is the Boss Vanderbilt, a bodhisattva predator Irraka of the Blood Talons. All the <i>magath</i> fearfully obey Boss Vanderbilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T09:03:41-07:00","id":1493734,"title":"","content":"Riiiiiise! Riiiiise, once more!<br /> <br /> 17)Sometimes, Uratha swimming out at sea find themselves pulled down by unseen currents, down and across the Gauntlet, then deeper still, to a crimson shore that is neither Shadow nor material. A tiny red sun, a dying ember, casts all under its crimson glare, bathing everything the color of blood. The beach these werewolves wash up on are eroded by sanguine waters, and, sometimes, worm-like <i>things</i> come up from the deep to feast on whatever they find ion the sore.<br /> <br /> Going inland only makes things worse, as it reveals an alien landscape of red plants with purple ichor, vast skeletons of upright-sitting creatures of unknown taxonomy, and rivers that stink of human feces. Eventually, one will find a great gore-covered toadstool, and, if a werewolf breathes in its spores, he then can return to the material universe\u2014-but carrying a deformed lamprey egg inside himself.<br /> <br /> 18)The Leaf Cathedral is found in the Shadow near the world\u2019s oldest Joshua tree, a 5,000-year-old vestige of an earlier time, before writing, before civilization. By stepping into the Shadow, this Joshua tree is beyond huge, with a labyrinth of ladders and steps carved into its bark. Solve this puzzle, and entrance to the Leaf Cathedral opens.<br /> <br /> A vast structure of odd angles, sharp turns and splinters waiting to strike, the Leaf Cathedral shifts due to the seasons.<br /> <br /> In spring, tiny flower-spirits take over, and make beer and dance and frolic.<br /> <br /> In summer, Helions descend and burn hot as the sun, but the Leaf Cathedral does not char. This infuriates the Helions, yet it has always been so.<br /> <br /> In autumn, a single harvest-spirit, Old Farmhand at the Edge of Town, moves in, driving the Helions out. He sleeps throughout his occupancy.<br /> <br /> And in winter, a door to inky oblivion opens, and, while nothing comes through, spirits abandon the Leaf Cathedral en mass. Whispers invite travelers to step inside. No one who obeys has ever seen again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-26-2022, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-27T09:25:11-07:00","id":1493833,"title":"","content":"19)There is a reason, Egyptian werewolves say, to avoid the ancient temple-city ruins like Crocodopolis. These places are inhabited in their Shadow opposite by sand-fleshed jackal-bodied spirits of Garm, bloody taloned sphinx priestesses of Ma\u2019at and animate hieroglyphs that screech mad meaning into the ears of passers by.<br /> <br /> But Crocodolis is the worst of them all, for something great and evil lurks here and considers wolfflesh a great delicacy. In the Shadow of Crocodopolis, crocodile-spirits of enormous size bedecked in gold and muddy saffron play subtle games of hunter and witchcraft with blind ibis-headed \u2018mummies\u2019, the winner devouring the loser. The statues of the gods are alive, sand pose riddles to passers by. Those who fail to answer properly get swept up....into a Place-That-Isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Serapis is an artificial god, created by the orders of the Greeks who conquered Egypt, yet Serapis has a blood existence, a spiritual chimera of different body parts all stitched together as one. In his temple, which cannot be escaped save by slaying the god, howling wind can be heard outside, with the mad echoing laughter of hyenas and the desperate cries for help from voices long silenced. Here, inside the Place-That-Isn\u2019t lay half-devoured fetishes that obey no laws of their ilk, as Serapis slowly eats them to fuel his own alien Essence. Where do these fetishes come from? No one knows.<br /> <br /> Serapis itself is a great god-beast, a spirit stitched together from mortal animal-parts and cast into Twilight. Egyptian werewolves have encountered such horrors before, but <i>never</i> on this <i>scale</i>. <br /> <br /> Serapis angrily laments his disobedience to Anubis, and curses his fate for being locked away, here. Werewolves who find themselves in Serapis\u2019 clutches must fight for their lives, as the bull-god command ushabti spirit warriors to attack intruders. Those who kill Serapis are cast by unseen hands back to the normal Shadow of Crocodopolis. Those who lose...are <i>never seen from again</i>.<br /> <br /> 20)Humans have uncovered a treasure, and both Forsaken and Pure viciously fight to control what mortalkind has unearthed.<br /> <br /> In South America, archaeologists recently dug up a complex mandala of stone, broken skulls, teeth made of obsidian and spirals upon spirals. It is the physically largest fetish on Earth, weighing thousands of tons.<br /> <br /> <i>...and there is a Place-That-Isn\u2019t inside the thing</i>. A place werewolves are eager to explore, for the fetish has somehow bound a <i>Royal Avatar</i>.<br /> <br /> Should an Uratha pack subdue the fetish and gain access to its inner world, they find themselves in a shining white labyrinth that blindingly reflects the light, making it nearly impossible to see. Vast Helions shaped like humanoid llamas wander to and fro carrying massive obsidian mallets; those they encounter, the Helions smash to pulp.<br /> <br /> The Royal Avatar, a goat-like humanoid of shining beauty and irradiating purity lies impaled at the heart of the labyrinth, bound by powerful rites. Free it, and the Place-That-Isn\u2019t vanishes. The giant stone fetish that once contained the Royal Avatar can now freely be used.<br /> <br /> 21)In the foothills of America\u2019s Appalachian Mountains, witches cavort with wolves, brewing strange concoctions made from moonshine, human fat and the blood of goats. Wolf-Blooded cultists and their Uratha kin worship at an ancient still from the 1920s, long since abandoned.<br /> <br /> At first, they rebuilt the still in hopes in hopes of making easy cash. But they had <i>dreams</i> out in the pristine forest and amidst the kudzu. These visions led them down esoteric alchemical paths, til they learnt to make witches\u2019 brew.<br /> <br /> This brew allows Wolf-Blooded to sidestep into the Shadow at loci, and allows werewolves to sidestep into the Shadow without the need for a locus. A powerful boon, indeed!<br /> <br /> But something lurks at the still, something intangible even by the standards of Twilight, and the witch-wolves soon found their way into a house somehow hidden <i>within</i> the kudzu, where spiders\u2014-but <i>not</i> Azlu!\u2014-made of dandelions and sawdust speak in eldritch riddles. The witch-wolves now bow low to these strangely fleshy things, in a Place-That-Isn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> And the brew demands a price of its own: a horrifying addiction that, given time, cause the Wolf-Blooded cultists to split open and birth more not-Azlu, while real Azlu find themselves strangely attracted to the cult\u2019s werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-27-2022, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T05:35:34-07:00","id":1493970,"title":"","content":"22)<b>Soulless Wolf</b>, like all Firstborn of Father Wolf, has <b>It\u2019s</b> own Place-That-Isn\u2019t, and this realm can only be found by going to the sites of humankind\u2019s deepest mines and furthest underground exploration. By chanting and bloodletting, self-flagellation and ritual torture, one will eventually find a crack in the deep earth....leading <i>down</i>. Down...to <b>it</b>.<br /> <br /> Fitting down this crack takes supernatural aid, as it is only a few inches wide. Unearthly sounds can be heard if one listens at this crack long enough: mad laughter, soft weeping, someone screaming for help, the sound of gunshots and beatings and even worse. All coming from <i>below</i>, ever <i>downwards</i>.<br /> <br /> Should one somehow manage to follow this crack in the Earth downwards, one would enter an upside world, with infinite inky oblivion below and torturous Labyrinthian paths above. Everything is <i>wrong</i>, in a way that\u2019s hard to define in any meaningful sense. From below bellows forth forlorn wolf-howls full of absolute despair.<br /> <br /> There are no inhabitants of the maze. It just goes <i>on and on</i>, never repeating itself twice. Many make it no further and slowly starve to death. <br /> <br /> Bizarre markings etch the wall, but they make no sense. No etchings in the First Tongue, but in a language nonetheless; it\u2019s just a language one must be mad and evil and depraved to have any hope of figuring out. Once deciphered, these messages lead down routes that are otherwise impossible to find or follow, til one reaches a deeper level altogether.<br /> <br /> As Above, So Below. To go down, one must go <i>up</i>. It is a contradiction, but it is nonetheless true. Crazed human cultists wander this hidden layer of the maze, their eyes gnawed out and their tongues removed. Freakish gargoyle-like spirits wander to and fro, and drag victims partially into the walls, where they suffocate to death. Hearths full of fire that burns but does not consume may be found here or there. Telephones connecting to <i>somewhere</i> dot the walls, connected to mysterious cable that one can\u2019t follow. Pick up a phone, and you\u2019ll hear something so terrible you\u2019ll ram pencils into your eardrums to make it stop.<br /> <br /> Shadows move and slither, angles are wrong, proportions are off, contradictory architecture everywhere. Passages don\u2019t lead the same way twice.<br /> <br /> Eventually, <b>it</b> finds all intruders. <b>Soulless Wolf</b> stalks the ceiling, <b>its</b> body turned inside out in grotesque parody of normal physiology. <b>It</b> will hunt you, but <b>it</b> won\u2019t harm you more than <b>it</b> must. <b>It\u2019s</b> <i>herding</i> you, you see, to an even deeper level. Those that go there never return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-29-2022, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T19:20:56-07:00","id":1494172,"title":"","content":"23)A pack discovers a gaping hole in the Gauntlet that they manage to make use of. They enter into a strange realm of fear, pain and creeping dread, wandering through hellish locales seemingly built to invoke as much fear as possible.<br /> <br /> And worse, this Place-That-Isn\u2019t is <i>inhabited</i> by creatures straight out of myth: ogres and giant human-faced spiders and killer dolls and frost-souled maidens and even roaring Greek chimeras. Sometimes, these monsters are little better than beasts, but, strangely, at other times their wits greatly increase.<br /> <br /> Wat do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T10:44:19-07:00","id":1494235,"title":"","content":"24)Even machine-spirits have Places-That-Aren\u2019t, it seems. By entering the Highhopfer building at exactly 11:11 pm, using elevator three and going to the following floors in the following order (10, 1, 1, 2, 22, 11), one finds oneself in a computer lab more advanced than anything the pack has <i>ever</i> seen before.<br /> <br /> Glowing computer screens calculate the orbits of every asteroid in the solar system, another computer keeps constant tabs of the exact numbers of pigeons in the city, while yet another records every game of Backgammon it can, by whatever means it can. This data is archived, then sent...<i>somewhere</i>.<br /> <br /> And then vaguely insectile machine-spirits unfold from the walls, whirring, flesh-tearing blades, armored chassises and magnetic rail guns, ready to destroy the intruders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T11:26:01-08:00","id":1496518,"title":"","content":"RIIIIISE, MY CHILD! RIIIIISE! LIVE, LIVE, LIVE!<br /> <br /> 25)Some Places-That-Aren\u2019t seem completely outside cosmology as werewolves understand it, and the Little Labyrinth is one such place.<br /> <br /> A glass labyrinth just large enough for a werewolf in wolf-shape to crawl through, made of glass with a strong, refreshing breeze running through from some unknowable distant place, the labyrinth is in the sky above an infinite plain of reeds and flooded farmland. The glass is unbreakable, and escaping to the sea of marshy reeds Below is impossible. Above, the sky is perpetually at night, with Luna absent entirely.<br /> <br /> Uratha who look at these stars long enough can invoke prophecies in themselves as Cahalith can.<br /> <br /> Below them, the fields are empty of spirits, though, occasionally, light will shine down from the infinite starry abyss, depositing a single man of Egyptian ethnicity, nude but otherwise healthy. He can\u2019t see the Uratha or the Little Labyrinth, and seems content to stare at the stars in wonder.<br /> <br /> Uratha here have a great, immense feeling this place is not for them. Most feel compelled to try to leave, though the strong willed can resist it.<br /> <br /> Getting to the Little Labyrinth happens when a Uratha shifts into a wolf and enters a cardboard \u2018maze\u2019 built by a young child in Egypt. The doorways in can\u2019t be forced open, and the Little Labyrinth eventually vomits an intruding werewolf back out.<br /> <br /> 26)Easily enterable, the Place-That-Isn\u2019t under Three Mile Island is a biotoxin dumpnest, full of irradiated monuments of cancer-ridden tissue, great pulsating zits the size of large dogs growing from the ground, and the constant sound of wheezing and labored breathing.<br /> <br /> Radiation-spirits abound, but take the form of hideously mutated zombies. They can only regain Essence through the consumption of sentient beings, be they spirit, mortal or otherwise. Surprisingly, these spirits are <i>not</i> Wounded, and prey upon Maeltinets and Bale Hounds as fervently as they do Pure and Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-08-2022, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T17:02:25-08:00","id":1496661,"title":"","content":"27)The Parisian central HQ of the Temple of Apollo has become larger on the inside than on the outside. Filled with temple enemies frozen as inanimate gold, with a mute Wolf-Blooded priest wearing a laurel of gold-plated copper, it turns in on itself like a strangely linear labyrinth that one nevertheless can\u2019t solve. In the Temple\u2019s center is a gold-spirit totem for the pack, resembling a sculpted Adonis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T18:50:50-08:00","id":1496768,"title":"","content":"The town of <i>Laguna Playa</i>, just south of the <i>City of Angels</i>.<br /> <br /> This is my incomplete map; it's based off of a sea-side town I lived in, years ago.; I have to add more sprites, but you can see the hills forming and the farming communities And yes, one day I will build the <i>City of Angels</i>. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://iili.io/yApD6N.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://iili.io/yApD6N.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://iili.io/yApD6N.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://iili.io/yApD6N.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T09:47:39-08:00","id":1498314,"title":"","content":"29)A strange Claimed \u2018immortal\u2019 (\u2018purified\u2019 in some unspecified manner) has tamed a colony of Termite Hosts and built herself quite a Place-That-Isn\u2019t in Yosemite Park. A cathedral of tunnels lined with fossilized bones, this nexus of Stone bodies could sustain thousands of people with its fungal crops\u2014-assuming the mega-Claimed in control of the whole thing cared to do so.<br /> <br /> 30)Norse werewolves claim to have found Jotunheim. A Place-That-Isn\u2019t bound behind ancient seals, past the stone archway that blocks the path is a vast frozen forest where giants roam. Some are spirits, to be clear, but others are shuddering Hive-Claimed behemoths and creatures of primeval fear drawn from deepest human prehistory, while still others appear spun from dreams.<br /> <br /> In Jotunheim, the jotnar gather, as word spreads of Ymir\u2019s inevitable return.<br /> <br /> [No.30 is directly based off of <i>very</i> cool work by Chris Allen, aka, Acrozatarim. I could fill an entire thread with ideas this fine fellow has cooked up!]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 11-29-2022, 04:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T14:29:58-08:00","id":1498471,"title":"","content":"31)Not all Places-That-Aren\u2019t are in the <i>Hisil</i>\u2014-sometimes, a pinched-off zone physical reality occurs, and some unknowable force seals it away.<br /> <br /> Such is the case of the Land of the Maggot Titans. Appearing for all intents and purposes as a sealed-off alternate timeline, this version of Earth is dominated by vast chthonic sea beasts, who rule over the land as part of a \u2018wicked tribe\u2019. Divided into squabbling factions, these fish-monsters proclaim themselves living gods, and exist in a sealed off timeline stretching from 1929 to 1950, when the alternate world ends in fire and cleansing light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}